        "Abstract_or_Key_Finding": "BOF slag has low hydraulic activity (gamma-C2S, RO phase) and free CaO/MgO expansion; EAF-C as cement replacement gives similar 28 d strength (10% replacement up to 27% higher at 3 d in one study), EAF-S 25% replacement lowers strength ~25-30%. LFS cement replacement lowers strength (8-46% loss at 10-40%), max ~30% suggested. EAF as aggregate generally raises compressive strength. Leaching generally within limits.",
